    "eval_seed": 0,
    "layout_folder": "Eval_Layout/RoboDojo/arx_x5/0",
    "ordinal_rule": "SeedManager.init_eval (env/seed_manager/seed_manager.py:33-43) sorts <task>_<n>.json numerically; the 55 files are numbered 0-54 without a gap, so ordinal n is <task>_<n>.json",
    "instruction_survey": "Of the 55 eval_seed-0 layouts, only 0, 7 and 41 render the reviewed instruction."
  },
  "decision": "A persistent session runs classify_objects_by_language as a three-round session (K = 3 rounds) on layouts 7 -> 41 -> 0 of eval_seed 0, the only layouts that render the reviewed instruction; round 3 replays the reviewed layout 0 by an accepted exception for this task only. This appendix extends the classify_objects_by_language review-v2 record to layouts 7 and 41 without changing its contract text, and binds each audited layout's object metadata.",
  "criteria": [
    "Instruction: gen_instruction (task/RoboDojo/tasks/classify_objects_by_language.py:104-120) names the category of each label group cat0, cat1 and cat2. RunSpec binds the record's layout-0 instruction as the policy task language and the worker refuses a round whose upstream instruction differs from it or from round 0, so a layout is schedulable only when it renders exactly the reviewed instruction. Of the 55 eval_seed-0 layouts only 0, 7 and 41 do (cat0 car, cat1 watch, cat2 wooden_toy); every audited row records the rendered text.",
    "Objects: every audited layout holds exactly the three Rigid groups cat0-cat2 that run_reward reads by label prefix, each of one category with two or three instances, and no other Rigid instance. The baskets basket0-basket2 (basket/2, /3, /4 at x = -0.28, 0 and 0.28) and the camera stand, and the Room, Table, Ground and Background sections, are JSON-equal to the reviewed layout 0.",
    "Contract text: clause 1 assigns each named category the basket the instruction names and defines left, middle and right in the world frame; it holds because every audited layout renders the same instruction and keeps the baskets at layout 0's poses (basket0 toward -X, basket1 between, basket2 toward +X), which is run_reward's cat_i-to-basket_i pairing. Clauses 2 and 3 are layout-independent. The text is unchanged.",
    "Evaluator assets: the record binds the metadata of every object instance of layout 0 (evaluator_dependencies). Each row binds the metadata of every object instance of its own layout (evaluator_asset_dependencies; the layout-0 row reproduces the record's set byte for byte), which RunSpec resolution discloses for the scheduled layouts and fresh preflight re-hashes with the record's own dependencies (fail closed).",
    "Asset load: no audited object has a missing, clamped or mismatched layout mass.",
    "Schedule exception: the third round replays the reviewed layout 0, because only layouts 0, 7 and 41 render the reviewed instruction; for this task only, a scheduled round need not differ from layout 0. The schedule still holds three distinct layouts, so no layout repeats within the session.",
    "Not a reachability review: whether an arm reaches each object is decided by the catalog review (computed spawn distances) and the scene smoke (scheduled_object_reach); fixtures and placement targets are not reach-checked."
  ],
